# Opening AutoMuseAI

- User preference: whenever opening a newer AutoMuseAI build, close older
  AutoMuseAI versions so the user cannot accidentally use the wrong window.
- Select the newest successfully built versioned EXE in `dist`, excluding
  installers and backup files; verify its version against `core/version.py`.
- Close old versions gracefully via their main windows. Allow running workers
  to stop/save normally; do not force-kill active generation or delete data.
- If graceful closure remains blocked, inspect the old window before claiming
  it is closed or starting competing jobs on the same browser profile.
- Launch from the `dist` working directory to preserve the user's configuration.
- Verify that the new version has a responding main window and that older
  versions have exited. Leave unrelated apps and browsers alone.
